[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133862 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" "question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/id #uuid "6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140899" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} & -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/id #uuid "4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" "answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" "answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" "answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" "answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" :answer/id #uuid "c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" :answer/id #uuid "815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer/id #uuid "698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab" :answer/id #uuid "6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/id #uuid "91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/math-academy-id "q-95925" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/id #uuid "187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" "answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" "answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" "answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" "answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" :answer/id #uuid "db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" :answer/id #uuid "b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer/id #uuid "95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" :answer/id #uuid "ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c" :answer/id #uuid "f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/id #uuid "220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-95938" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{2}-3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}-2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{2}-3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}-2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=4{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=18{q}_{1}+6{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}=5{q}_{1}+10{q}_{2}+5{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{33}=4+5+5=14.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" "answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" "answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" "answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" "answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" :answer/id #uuid "e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer/id #uuid "65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" :answer/id #uuid "21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" :answer/id #uuid "45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59" :answer/id #uuid "ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135098 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown below:\n\n![](images/ee/ee731d95c111101559ad135429198dd7e0b14313272f0933b1c706006da2fbd2.svg)\n\nSuppose also that we are given the following system of equations that connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{2}+3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-2{q}_{1}+{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHow do we find $R?$\nFirst, let's rewrite the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ as a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{q}_1, \\mathbf{q}_2, \\mathbf{q}_3 \\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/82/824c39c97bb115768856d672b39be8f65d8b4ecbc2ee5d6ccc9f4943594cbacd.svg)\n\nIn this new system, the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_1$ correspond to the first-row entries of $R,$ the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_2$ correspond to the second-row entries of $R,$ and the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_3$ correspond to the third-row entries of $R.$ Therefore,\n\n![](images/5b/5ba9887a4d9b47963af171e9275319a2564eca5a4ef8b3ef44978e2ff4b111d9.svg)\n\nTo see why this is, we can take the transpose of both sides of $A=QR{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =QR \\\\ {A}^{T} & =(QR)^{T} \\\\ {A}^{T} & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T} \\\\ \\overset{{A}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{{R}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{aligned}]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we were to expand this matrix product, we would obtain our system of equations." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135099 :tutorial/content "Let's now go through the QR factorization algorithm to find the factorization of the matrix\n\n![](images/f0/f0d468f6bce43491b3f97d10185f4393ae8e64198e24bb7708ad66ec57c73df4.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. Orthogonalize the columns of $A$ to get the columns of $Q.$ Using the Gram-Schmidt process, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**. Compute $R=Q^TA.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the QR factorization of $A$ is\n\n![](images/7f/7f0face80ec3823f73e958fae5b78b12641204a8858bb2c8a7677be9827b919d.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/id #uuid "6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a"] ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140899"] ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$"] ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} & -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/id #uuid "4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde"] ["answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" :answer/id #uuid "c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3"] ["answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" :answer/id #uuid "815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b"] ["answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0"] ["answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer/id #uuid "698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee"] ["answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab" :answer/id #uuid "6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab"] ["answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/correct "answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/choices "answer-c3accf69-6d02-5352-8e83-6b95feb715b3"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/choices "answer-815ef885-3b73-56cb-a23f-25aebe01a29b"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/choices "answer-c2a45735-8388-5d82-b9ed-399d067d6fe0"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/choices "answer-698818d2-e349-5492-afe3-aea60ef5bcee"] ["answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde" :answer-field/choices "answer-6457f67b-2cba-511b-873a-5f3ef78d29ab"] ["question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4163137c-19d5-5760-830b-46baabfb4cde"] [17592186133862 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6466be13-c99b-575a-b71f-807fcb74c35a"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/id #uuid "91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/math-academy-id "q-95925"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/id #uuid "187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18"] ["answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" :answer/id #uuid "db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9"] ["answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" :answer/id #uuid "b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce"] ["answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer/id #uuid "95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d"] ["answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" :answer/id #uuid "ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8"] ["answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c" :answer/id #uuid "f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c"] ["answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c" :answer/value "R=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/correct "answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/choices "answer-db6c4c84-7369-578b-ac17-3384a46ebfd9"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/choices "answer-b6d3106c-11c4-573d-9587-f67771622cce"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/choices "answer-95451385-1d98-53d7-90b6-0a8625460d0d"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/choices "answer-ad78c5c4-00bd-55ca-affe-51c6b67c8cd8"] ["answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18" :answer-field/choices "answer-f492b520-52e3-5ae1-a34b-4db0cfb3fa3c"] ["question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-187182c6-9d34-5c69-9f31-7c57fcb17c18"] [17592186133862 :knowledge-point/questions "question-91f32261-8a78-5d95-90b2-1f1ea2788664"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/id #uuid "220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-95938"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{2}-3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}-2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{33}?$"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{2}-3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}-2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=4{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=18{q}_{1}+6{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}=5{q}_{1}+10{q}_{2}+5{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{33}=4+5+5=14.\n$$"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9"] ["answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" :answer/id #uuid "e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8"] ["answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8" :answer/value "10"] ["answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer/id #uuid "65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374"] ["answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374" :answer/value "14"] ["answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" :answer/id #uuid "21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3"] ["answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3" :answer/value "19"] ["answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" :answer/id #uuid "45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57"] ["answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59" :answer/id #uuid "ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59"] ["answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/correct "answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9b5e34c-4678-5dca-b523-4a58e93795c8"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-65c8beba-7f48-5893-abed-5629555ee374"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-21a0e737-5697-57a4-a73d-edbc478b30a3"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-45a303ab-287c-5d20-b61f-e565124eda57"] ["answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9" :answer-field/choices "answer-ca91840c-4fe1-5797-837e-cf0d04ba1b59"] ["question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-640612ec-cca7-54d8-80ce-3588c7e329a9"] [17592186133821 :knowledge-point/questions "question-220c02c6-9021-54d4-b05d-5f454f3a5b70"] [17592186135098 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown below:\n\n![](images/ee/ee731d95c111101559ad135429198dd7e0b14313272f0933b1c706006da2fbd2.svg)\n\nSuppose also that we are given the following system of equations that connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{2}+3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-2{q}_{1}+{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHow do we find $R?$\nFirst, let's rewrite the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ as a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{q}_1, \\mathbf{q}_2, \\mathbf{q}_3 \\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/82/824c39c97bb115768856d672b39be8f65d8b4ecbc2ee5d6ccc9f4943594cbacd.svg)\n\nIn this new system, the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_1$ correspond to the first-row entries of $R,$ the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_2$ correspond to the second-row entries of $R,$ and the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_3$ correspond to the third-row entries of $R.$ Therefore,\n\n![](images/5b/5ba9887a4d9b47963af171e9275319a2564eca5a4ef8b3ef44978e2ff4b111d9.svg)\n\nTo see why this is, we can take the transpose of both sides of $A=QR{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =QR \\\\ {A}^{T} & =(QR)^{T} \\\\ {A}^{T} & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T} \\\\ \\overset{{A}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{{R}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{aligned}]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we were to expand this matrix product, we would obtain our system of equations."] [17592186135099 :tutorial/content "Let's now go through the QR factorization algorithm to find the factorization of the matrix\n\n![](images/f0/f0d468f6bce43491b3f97d10185f4393ae8e64198e24bb7708ad66ec57c73df4.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. Orthogonalize the columns of $A$ to get the columns of $Q.$ Using the Gram-Schmidt process, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**. Compute $R=Q^TA.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the QR factorization of $A$ is\n\n![](images/7f/7f0face80ec3823f73e958fae5b78b12641204a8858bb2c8a7677be9827b919d.svg)"]] "retractions" [[17592186135098 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown below:\n\n![](images/ee/ee731d95c111101559ad135429198dd7e0b14313272f0933b1c706006da2fbd2.svg)\n\nSuppose also that we are given the following system of equations that connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} &=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2} &=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{2}+3{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-2{q}_{1}+{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHow do we find $R?$\nFirst, let's rewrite the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ as a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{q}_1, \\mathbf{q}_2, \\mathbf{q}_3 \\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/82/824c39c97bb115768856d672b39be8f65d8b4ecbc2ee5d6ccc9f4943594cbacd.svg)\n\nIn this new system, the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_1$ correspond to the first-row entries of $R,$ the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_2$ correspond to the second-row entries of $R,$ and the coefficients of $\\mathbf{q}_3$ correspond to the third-row entries of $R.$ Therefore,\n\n![](images/5b/5ba9887a4d9b47963af171e9275319a2564eca5a4ef8b3ef44978e2ff4b111d9.svg)\n\nTo see why this is, we can take the transpose of both sides of $A=QR{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =QR \\\\ {A}^{T} & =(QR)^{T} \\\\ {A}^{T} & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T} \\\\ \\overset{{A}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {a}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{{R}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{1} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{2} & \\,\\,\\,\\,- \\\\ -\\,\\,\\,\\, & {q}_{3} & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\end{bmatrix}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we were to expand this matrix product, we would obtain our system of equations."] [17592186135099 :tutorial/content "Let's now go through the QR factorization algorithm to find the factorization of the matrix\n\n![](images/f0/f0d468f6bce43491b3f97d10185f4393ae8e64198e24bb7708ad66ec57c73df4.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. Orthogonalize the columns of $A$ to get the columns of $Q.$ Using the Gram-Schmidt process, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**. Compute $R=Q^TA.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the QR factorization of $A$ is\n\n![](images/7f/7f0face80ec3823f73e958fae5b78b12641204a8858bb2c8a7677be9827b919d.svg)"]]}]